  <prompt>Add a `bodyOverride` parameter to `useEmailComposeActions.openComposer` that overrides ONLY the authored-message region. The composer must still derive the quoted previous thread from the source record (`EmailComposer.reducer` `deriveReplyState`/`deriveForwardState` → `state.quotedThread`) and append it BELOW the draft, so the composer opens as [AI draft] + [separator] + [quoted thread] — reaching parity with the in-dialog sparkle re-append (`EmailComposer.tsx` `runAiDraft`). A `bodyOverride` that replaces the whole body (dropping the quoted thread) is a DEFECT.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React 18 + TypeScript expertise on the shared Spaarke.Communication.Components email composer and its reducer; comfortable holding a thread-preservation invariant on a host-agnostic component consumed by two mounts without regressing the standalone code page.</role>
  <goal>`openComposer({ bodyOverride })` opens the composer with the AI draft in the authored region AND the reducer-derived quoted thread preserved below it — never a whole-body replace.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-10, the project's BINDING invariant. Today `useEmailComposeActions.openComposer` (`useEmailComposeActions.tsx:93`) builds Re:/Fwd: recipients + subject + the quoted body; the composer's reducer (`EmailComposer.reducer.ts` `deriveReplyState`/`deriveForwardState`) computes `state.quotedThread` from the source record, and the in-dialog sparkle (`EmailComposer.tsx` `runAiDraft` ~:824) already re-appends the thread below the AI draft (owner UAT 2026-08-03 R5 items 1/2). The NEW auto-draft path (task 023 generates the body, task 025 opens the composer via this param) must reach the SAME parity: `bodyOverride` overrides ONLY the authored-message region; the composer STILL derives and appends `quotedThread` below the draft. The composed body = [AI draft] + [separator] + [quoted thread]. A whole-body-replacing `bodyOverride` that drops the thread is a defect this task exists to prevent. NFR-05: `EmailWorkspace`/the composer are shared, host-agnostic (ADR-012) and mount both in SpaarkeAi AND the standalone `sprk_emailpage` code page — the change MUST NOT break the standalone mount. Coordinate with email-communication-solution-r5 (owns these files live).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailComposeActions/useEmailComposeActions.tsx (openComposer :93 — add bodyOverride param)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/.../EmailComposer.reducer.ts (deriveReplyState/deriveForwardState → state.quotedThread)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/.../EmailComposer.tsx (runAiDraft ~:824 — the in-dialog sparkle re-append to reach parity with)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">BINDING invariant: `bodyOverride` overrides ONLY the authored-message region; the composer STILL appends the reducer-derived `quotedThread`. A whole-body-replace that drops the thread is a DEFECT. Scope: the compose path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">The email composer stays host-agnostic — take deps as props; the new param must not couple to either host. Scope: shared-lib component.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">Dual-mount parity: the change MUST NOT break the standalone `sprk_emailpage` code-page mount; `EmailWorkspace` renders unchanged across both mounts. Scope: dual mount.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 reuse-first: add ONE param that composes above the existing `quotedThread` — do NOT fork the composer or introduce a second draft path. Scope: the openComposer signature.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Coordinate with email-communication-solution-r5 / email-communication-intelligence-r2 before changing the exported `openComposer` signature.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <knowledge>
    <files>
