  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Trace the existing compose path: `openComposer` (:93) → reducer `deriveReplyState`/`deriveForwardState` → `state.quotedThread`; and the in-dialog `runAiDraft` re-append (~:824) that this must reach parity with.</step>
    <step order="2">Add a `bodyOverride?` parameter to `openComposer` that seeds ONLY the authored-message region of the initial composer state.</step>
    <step order="3">Ensure the reducer STILL derives `quotedThread` from the source record and the composed body is [bodyOverride draft] + [separator] + [quotedThread] — identical structure to the sparkle re-append.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify the standalone `sprk_emailpage` mount still opens/renders unchanged (dual-mount parity).</step>
    <step order="5">Add a reducer/unit test asserting the composed body contains BOTH the draft AND the `quotedThread` block; add a negative test where a whole-body-replace would fail.</step>
    <step order="6">npm run build the Spaarke.Communication.Components package (+ SpaarkeAi if consumed); update TASK-INDEX.</step>
  </steps>
  <escalation>
    <trigger>If preserving the quoted thread cannot be reconciled with the auto-draft body without either forking the composer or dropping the thread, STOP and escalate (FR-10 BINDING invariant, data-loss-adjacent) rather than shipping a whole-body-replace. Coordinate the `openComposer` signature change with email-communication-solution-r5 before merging.</trigger>
  </escalation>
  <justification>
    <existing>`useEmailComposeActions.openComposer` (:93) exists and already builds recipients + subject + quoted body via the reducer's `quotedThread`.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — add ONE `bodyOverride` param that composes above the existing reducer-derived `quotedThread`; no new draft path.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Auto-draft (task 025) either cannot inject a body or clobbers the quoted thread — the exact invariant this project exists to hold fails (owner UAT R5 items 1/2 regress).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>
