  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`openComposer({ bodyOverride })` seeds only the authored-message region; the composer opens as [AI draft] + [separator] + [quoted thread].</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A reducer/unit test asserts the composed body contains BOTH the AI draft AND the reducer-derived `quotedThread` block.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a `bodyOverride` that replaces the whole body (dropping the quoted thread) FAILS the test (defect asserted against).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reply and Forward both preserve their respective `quotedThread` (deriveReplyState / deriveForwardState).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the standalone `sprk_emailpage` mount opens/renders unchanged (dual-mount parity intact).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Spaarke.Communication.Components builds; unit tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>FR-10 BINDING invariant; reaches parity with the shipped in-dialog sparkle re-append (`runAiDraft` ~:824). Consumed by task 025 (Reply/Reply All/Forward cards). Coordinate the `openComposer` signature with email-communication-solution-r5. NFR-05 dual-mount parity is a hard gate.</notes>
